vine 1.2.0
prefix: transport
title: Transport and journal layer
---
[root] Canonical transport and journal layer (complete)
Define the reusable logical layer shared by local input, replay input, and future network input. Keep source transport metadata separate from semantic observations, preserve explicit identity and order, and coordinate immutable journal/branch publication without making transport metadata authoritative game time.
Files: transport.vine; proposals/transport-and-journal.md; proposals/input-and-interaction.md; proposals/presentation-host.md; crates/caravan-demo/src/input.rs; crates/caravan-demo/src/orchestrator.rs; crates/engine-journal/**; crates/engine-branches/**; tests/**
Do: Settle the ordered batch, membership-view, transport-envelope, and journal-operation boundaries before extracting reusable engine APIs. Preserve the current InputPacketSet prototype as a derived specialization while recording the migration evidence required for ordered/repeated observations.
Accept: One canonical proposal owns the reusable transport/journal semantics; source adapters, Stage/Orchestrator, JournalWriter, branches, and host byte/storage ports have disjoint responsibilities; the current prototype remains behaviorally covered; and the next implementation packet has deterministic identity/order and late-publication acceptance evidence.
-> batch-model
-> buffer-lifecycle
-> journal-operations
-> transport-contract
-> transport-evidence
